-- Q13 [Adrenal Glands] medium skill2 ans=D
WITH q AS (
  INSERT INTO questions (section, topic, subtopic, question_text, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, foundation, content_category, discipline, cognitive_skill, estimated_time_seconds, figure_svg)
  VALUES ('bio_biochem', 'The Endocrine System', 'Adrenal Glands', 'The adrenal cortex is arranged in three concentric zones, each specializing in one class of steroid hormone. A toxin selectively destroys only the deepest cortical zone, the layer lying just outside the medulla. Which hormones'' production is most directly lost?', '[{"label": "A", "text": "Catecholamines"}, {"label": "B", "text": "Mineralocorticoids"}, {"label": "C", "text": "Glucocorticoids"}, {"label": "D", "text": "Adrenal androgens"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'This is a Biology question that falls under the content category ''Endocrine System: Hormones and Their Sources.''

The answer is D because the three zones of the adrenal cortex are layered outer to inner as the zona glomerulosa (mineralocorticoids), the zona fasciculata (glucocorticoids), and the deepest zona reticularis, which produces the adrenal androgens. Destroying only the deepest zone therefore removes androgen production.

(Choice D) is correct: the zona reticularis is the deepest cortical zone and is the source of the adrenal androgens, so its destruction most directly abolishes androgen output.

(Choice B) is incorrect: mineralocorticoids such as aldosterone come from the OUTERMOST zone, the zona glomerulosa, which the toxin spares.

(Choice C) is incorrect: glucocorticoids such as cortisol come from the MIDDLE zone, the zona fasciculata, not the deepest layer.

(Choice A) is incorrect: catecholamines are made by the adrenal MEDULLA, not by any zone of the cortex, so they are not a cortical-zone product at all.

This Skill 2 item requires mapping the described cortical-zone position (deepest, adjacent to the medulla) onto the specific steroid class that zone produces.', 'medium', '3A', 'Endocrine System: Hormones and Their Sources', 'biology', 2, 75, NULL)
  RETURNING id
)
